{"id": 23, "ts": 1781187028.4033659, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s conscientiousness and stress resilience, but I\u2019m less convinced that B remains the strongest overall given the gaps we\u2019ve identified. We have no evidence of B\u2019s attention\u2011to\u2011detail (memory for numbers) and his documented uncooperative, pretentious demeanor could undermine crew cooperation on long\u2011haul flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC brings concrete strengths that directly address several safety\u2011critical criteria: he is \u201cknown to be\u202f100\u202f% reliable,\u201d consistently creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, and \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly.\u201d Those facts speak to operational reliability, crew cooperation, and decision quality\u2014core requirements for a long\u2011distance pilot. While C\u2019s communication style and reluctance to further education are concerns, they appear less severe than B\u2019s uncooperative attitude and the unknown risk to information accuracy. Therefore, I shift my provisional vote to Candidate\u202fC, believing his proven reliability and decision\u2011making outweigh the unresolved issues with B."}
